# Pairs with TailMonotone. The pre-#5810 phase-2 commit: no fence, and TAIL is
# written with a blind upsert of the higher of the batch's end and the
# instance's own highest commit. A stale predecessor's late batch below the
# successor's committed tail regresses TAIL.
MODULE: TailMonotoneStaleWriterBlindUpsert
TARGET: TailMonotone
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: a stale predecessor's commit blind-upserts TAIL from its own high-water mark
PERTURBS: LateLand

--- FIND
       THEN IF /\ o >= tail
               /\ prevFresh
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the predecessor's commit is not conditional on its view of TAIL.
       THEN IF /\ o >= tail
--- END

--- FIND
                 /\ ct' = Max({ct, o})
                 /\ curFresh' = FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: TAIL is upserted from the predecessor's own highest commit.
                 /\ ct' = Max({p \in Offs : occ[p] \in {"ackedPrev", "latePrev", "dup"}} \cup {-1, o})
                 /\ curFresh' = FALSE
--- END
--- FIND
WithCrossSiloMove == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: raises the bound so a lost activation may move to another silo.
WithCrossSiloMove == TRUE
--- END
